> Also after internal discussion, we concluded that `ansible_network_os=auto` feature will be deprecated and removed in 2.10. 

Okay, will remove the code in my collection avoiding confusion. Indeed, you are right that most people will have the correct `network_os` in their inventory. I would just curious about the correct implementation, as we've decided to make Nokia SR OS two different devices: `nokia.sros.classic` and `nokia.sros.md`. Since 2 years operators have the choice to use either classic or model-driven mode - which is a significant change as model-driven mode comes with a new CLI engine called MD-CLI and NETCONF support. So idea was to use `auto` to automatically select the `classic` or `md` plugins.
